Use the following color pallatte
Core Palette (Neutral, Professional, Premium)
Primary Backgrounds
Soft Off-White — #F7F8FA
Clean, modern, less harsh than pure white.
Pure White (cards / surfaces) — #FFFFFF
Use for cards, sections, modals.
Primary Text
Charcoal Black — #1F2933
Headlines, primary copy. Softer than pure black, more premium.
Muted Gray — #6B7280
Secondary text, descriptions, labels.
Borders & Dividers
Light Neutral Gray — #E5E7EB
Dividers, subtle outlines, card borders.
Primary Accent (CTA / Links)
Deep Slate Blue — #1E40AF
This is your authority color.
CTAs
Links
Active states
Why blue?
Trusted
B2B-friendly
Universally accepted in US markets
Secondary Accent (Subtle Highlights)
Soft Steel Blue — #93C5FD
Hover states, icons, micro-interactions.
Success / Confirmation
Muted Emerald — #047857
Checkmarks, confirmations, positive signals.
Not neon. Not loud. Professional.
How to use this palette (this matters more than the colors)
60–30–10 Rule
60% → Off-white / white backgrounds
30% → Charcoal + muted gray text
10% → Accent colors (blue + green)
Most “cheap-looking” sites break this rule.
CTA styling (very important)
Primary CTA:
Background: #1E40AF
Text: #FFFFFF
Border radius: subtle (6–8px)
No gradients
Hover:
Darken slightly → #1E3A8A
